1. Educational & Reference Use
Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person or robotics team obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files
to view, study, and learn from the code for educational and reference purposes. 

You are welcome to analyze the structure, PID implementations, subsystem logic, and PROS/LemLib setups contained within this repository to understand 
how competitive VEX V5 software is organized.

2. Competition Usage & VEX Rule Compliance Notice
Direct competition use (copying and pasting this codebase onto a competition robot) is strongly discouraged, as every robot has unique gear ratios, 
motor placements, wheel sizes, sensor offsets, and weight distributions. Running this code directly on a different chassis will likely result in erratic 
movements, stall lockouts, or hardware damage.

Also, in accordance with official VEX Robotics Competition rules regarding Student-Centered Design and Code Originality, all competition software must 
represent the skill level, design, and engineering strengths of the students on that specific team. Submitting unoriginal or blindly copied code violates 
the spirit and rules of the competition.

3. Attribution
If you use concepts, helper functions, or structural layouts inspired by this repository in your own project, please provide proper credit to 
13155U in your engineering notebook and code comments.
